From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 17:07:47 +0200
Subject: MIPS: intel-mips: enable PCIe in grx500_defconfig

The xRX500 root complexes and the slim PHY that feeds them are now
described in the SoC dtsi and driven by pcie-intel-gw.c and
phy-intel-grx500-pcie.c, but none of it is reachable from a defconfig
kernel: MIPS only gets a PCI bus if CONFIG_PCI is stated, and both
drivers sit behind menus that default off.

 - CONFIG_PCI. INTEL_MIPS selects HAVE_PCI and PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC, but
   HAVE_PCI only makes the PCI menu visible -- the bus itself is a plain
   prompt with no default, so without this line the whole subsystem,
   including drivers/pci/controller/, is compiled out.

 - CONFIG_PCI_MSI, which is what makes CONFIG_PCIE_INTEL_GW selectable
   at all: it "depends on PCI_MSI", and PCI_MSI has no default, so
   asking for PCIE_INTEL_GW without it is silently dropped by
   olddefconfig rather than reported.

   This host bridge has no MSI: the four INTx lines reach the GIC over
   their own interrupt-map entries and the DesignWare iMSI-RX block is
   deliberately left alone by the driver's .msi_init hook, which clears
   pp->has_msi_ctrl and so keeps both dw_pcie_msi_host_init() and the
   MSI register programming in dw_pcie_msi_init() out of the picture.
   PCI_MSI=y is therefore configuration-only. The bridge advertises no
   MSI domain and does not set PCI_BUS_FLAGS_NO_MSI, so an endpoint
   driver that asks for MSI lands in the PCI_MSI_ARCH_FALLBACKS path
   that arch/mips/Kconfig turns on, where the __weak arch_setup_msi_irq()
   returns -EINVAL; pci_enable_msi() fails cleanly and every well-behaved
   driver falls back to INTx, which is the wiring that exists.

 - CONFIG_PCIE_INTEL_GW for the root complexes, which pulls in
   PCIE_DW_HOST and the DesignWare core underneath it.

 - CONFIG_PHY_INTEL_GRX500_PCIE for the slim PHY. It selects GENERIC_PHY,
   MFD_SYSCON and RESET_CONTROLLER on its own; the latter two are already
   on from the INTEL_MIPS selects.

CONFIG_PCIEPORTBUS stays off. The port services it would bind -- AER,
PME, hotplug -- are all things this application block latches in IRNCR
and that the driver deliberately leaves masked and unrequested, so
enabling portdrv would buy nothing but a level line nobody clears.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
index 50280ffee7df..98f812230054 100644
--- a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
@@ -73,6 +73,9 @@ CONFIG_IP6_NF_TARGET_REJECT=m
 CONFIG_IP6_NF_MANGLE=m
 CONFIG_ATM=m
 CONFIG_ATM_BR2684=m
+CONFIG_PCI=y
+CONFIG_PCI_MSI=y
+CONFIG_PCIE_INTEL_GW=y
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM=y
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM_COUNT=4
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM_SIZE=8192
@@ -107,6 +110,7 @@ CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_NETDEV=y
 # CONFIG_MIPS_PLATFORM_DEVICES is not set
 CONFIG_INTEL_CGU_CLK=y
 # CONFIG_IOMMU_SUPPORT is not set
+CONFIG_PHY_INTEL_GRX500_PCIE=y
 # CONFIG_MANDATORY_FILE_LOCKING is not set
 CONFIG_QUOTA=y
 # CONFIG_PRINT_QUOTA_WARNING is not set
